# A173 — a refused attachment change reported as success (2026-09-15T15:36:28Z)

## 1. the finding's stated cause, and what the code actually does
$ git show HEAD:Sources/ChatBotsCore/ConversationEngine.swift | grep -n 'func setAttachments' -A 5
  1059:    public func setAttachments(_ documents: [AttachedDocument]) -> Bool {
  1060-        // Allowed *before* a conversation starts, and refused once one has. The task is
  1061-        // non-nil only while a turn is running, so requiring it to be nil would have made
  1062-        // this succeed precisely in the case it is meant to refuse and fail otherwise.
  1063-        guard turnsCompleted == 0, generationTask == nil else { return false }
  1064-        conversation.attachments = documents
$ git show HEAD:Sources/ChatBotsCore/EngineService.swift | grep -n 'setAttachments'
  182:            engine.setAttachments(engine.attachments.filter { $0.id.uuidString != id })
  186:            engine.setAttachments([])
  468:            engine.setAttachments(engine.attachments + [document])
$ git show HEAD:Sources/ChatBotsApp/Views/AttachmentBar.swift | grep -n 'disabled'
  26:            .disabled(!controller.canAttachFiles)
  157:            .disabled(false)
  (the engine refuses the change; the service discards the false and answers with a state;
   the app's x is always enabled — so a click did nothing and the page, which gated on the
   engine's own flag, was the only front end that agreed with it)

